 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "No motif on Maryam, the angels, Isa or the cradle. geometric on 42:6, a scroll for the revealed news of the unseen, a pen for the casting of pens. 42:10-12 quotes As-Sa'di's two readings (her time or absolutely) instead of taking one. 45: short-word flag at 45:20 (70 ms, listen). STAGING v4: 42-43 and 45-46: Maryam is only the green drop labelled Maryam in her place of prayer (As-Sa'di on 37: she kept to her mihrab), the angels ONE gold drop with the plural label that speaks (42:2, 43:1, 45:2...). Her drop glows only away from the Name and from the announcement of the birth (no glow on 42:5-6, 45:5-14 or the cradle 46:4); on the command 43:2-7 it glows (no group of worshippers is drawn for 43:6-7). Isa, the cradle and Jibril are not drawn; the glad tidings are a light plate only. 44: the people in charge of the Temple at a river (As-Sa'di: they cast their pens into the river) as an uncountable group of men; they speak and dispute; Zakariya, a blue drop, glows on 44:14 (both tafsirs: the lot fell to him); scroll plate for the revealed news of the unseen and pen plate for the casting of pens (ended before 44:15). The Prophet is not shown. Wide shots only in every drop chapter."
 },
